DESCRIPTION:Discovery Days is an early childhood program that encourages children ages 2 to 6 and their caregivers to have fun together through educational\, hands-on art\, music\, and movement activities. When you attend Discovery Days at the Longmont Museum with your child\, you will help them cultivate important school-readiness skills\, such as language development\, attention\, concentration\, fine motor skills\, emotional regulation\, and play and social abilities.\nOccurs weekly on Tuesdays Jan. 13-May 5\, 2026. Three 45 minute-1 hour sessions available: 9:15am\, 10:45am\, and 1pm.\nAttend a session that fits your schedule\, no registration needed. Learn more online and explore weekly themes at https://longmontcolorado.gov/museum/education/discovery-days/ or by calling 303-651-8374.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/discovery-days-music-and-movement-with-ms-ragen-5
DTEND:20260414T200000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Museum
DTSTART:20260414T151500Z
SUMMARY:🎵 Discovery Days: Music & Movement with Ms. Ragen
UID:68e32f30-21e9-49ec-9519-303eeb490e58@68e3.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Featuring Abigail Nims\, Mezzo-Soprano | This exciting program\, inspired by vocal music\, features a world premiere for large orchestra by the Italian composer Massimiliano Messieri. He will join Maestro Moore for a pre-concert talk at 6 PM. The concert also includes mezzo-soprano Abigail Nims performing Amy Beach’s Wand’ring Clouds\, which was the first composition by a woman to be performed by the Symphony Society of New York in 1892. Additionally\, Vaughan Williams' stunning and spiritual blend of ancient and modern elements is showcased in Fantasia on a Theme by Thomas Tallis\, which features two string orchestras. Finally\, Respighi’s Pines of Rome promises to be a sonic spectacle not to be missed!\nJoin us for the Pre-Concert Talk at 6pm.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/lso-concert-pines-of-rome-and-a-world-premiere
DTEND:20260412T030000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART:20260412T010000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Classical] LSO Concert Pines of Rome & a World Premiere
UID:1b16ab0a-25a1-4716-8e1c-30267ea91991@1b16.org
END:VEVENT
