DESCRIPTION:For more than 20 years\, The Hummin’ Birds have been bringing the spirit of early American music to life. Born out of Minnesota’s bluegrass and old-time scene\, Cami Harris and Mike Silbernagel honed their sound through late-night jams and festival campfires before winning first place in a 2006 Minnesota State Fair duet contest. Now based in Denver\, the duo shares their signature harmonies\, timeless song interpretations\, and heartfelt originals with audiences across the Front Range and Midwest.\nThis concert is part of the Longmont Museum’s Friday Afternoon Concert Series.  Enjoy an afternoon of live music in our Stewart Auditorium this fall featuring an eclectic array of musical acts from up and down the Front Range.\nLearn more and buy tickets online at https://longmontcolorado.gov/event/the-hummin-birds/ or by calling 303-651-8374.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/friday-afternoon-concert-the-hummin-birds
DTEND:20260410T223000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Museum
DTSTART:20260410T203000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Folk/Acoustic] Friday Afternoon Concert: The Hummin’ Birds
UID:bd4c645f-3b45-4cb9-af8e-00dcf84bfd80@bd4c.org
END:VEVENT
